#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186241086 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119798 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d216cc0e-58a7-5fab-b5fe-60c7656338cc" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Missing Numbers in the Matrix L of an LU Factorization"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a48f9b7-a09f-5e59-8fbc-b60875dc0064" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238427} {:answer/id #uuid "7e07e1ff-90d7-55c6-8187-bec87865fc6b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239150} {:answer/id #uuid "9142a26c-af0c-5413-a0a8-72e45c9c7f3e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239313} {:answer/id #uuid "a96a25da-05e1-5db0-812c-8666e834a401" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239540} {:answer/id #uuid "fbc2a1b3-578b-5f36-8343-25768d288491" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240280}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9142a26c-af0c-5413-a0a8-72e45c9c7f3e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239313} :answer-field/id #uuid "1474ec70-d403-5756-bc8f-af2e58baecae" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240361}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ca032623-0a65-5d05-a582-2e903aa5c322" :question/math-academy-id "q-105601" :question/problem "$$\n{{\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 7 & -5 \\\\ -4 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 8 & -4 & 7\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{A}={{\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & \\boxed{} & 1\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{L}\\cdot {{\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 7 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 9 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 9\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{U}\n$$\n\nConsider the LU factorization of the matrix $A$ above. What is the value of the entry ${l}_{32}$ in the matrix $L?$" :question/worked-solution "The matrix $U$ in the LU decomposition is obtained from the original matrix $A$ by row-reducing using Gaussian elementation. In particular, to make zeros below the main diagonal, we proceed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 7 & -5 \\\\ -4 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 8 & -4 & 7\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+1{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 7 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 9 & -4 \\\\ 8 & -4 & 7\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 7 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 9 & -4 \\\\ 0 & -18 & 17\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we want to make $0$ at the position ${a}_{32}$ using Gaussian elimination. To do this, we take the $3$rd row of $A,$ and we add the $2$nd row of $A$ multiplied by $2:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 7 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 9 & -4 \\\\ 0 & -18 & 17\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 7 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 9 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 9\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe entry ${l}_{32}$ of the matrix $L$ is the factor next to ${R}_{2},$ taken with the opposite sign:\n\n$$\n{l}_{32}=-(2)=-2.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302306 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119885 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e28bd3d9-649d-5cc3-a12e-e1f821caaf24" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the LU Factorization of a 3x3 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "81169e7e-75ed-5dae-9ca0-032d0842dc35" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300600} {:answer/id #uuid "d9529795-3b08-5aa4-9f38-dcfb6e621af0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301040} {:answer/id #uuid "de03b23a-7349-5ec1-ae5e-bf160aabe825" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301062} {:answer/id #uuid "e844b2ca-59c2-5351-a493-09f58e28c726" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301111} {:answer/id #uuid "fa2b4fbe-08a5-57db-b008-9b8089dd151b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301197}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d9529795-3b08-5aa4-9f38-dcfb6e621af0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301040} :answer-field/id #uuid "fb0c24f7-77bd-55d9-98c4-2e653e7b9496" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302029}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b6b690f5-c73e-55f2-9a04-9d767e300105" :question/math-academy-id "q-32652" :question/problem "$$\nD=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & -4 & 4 \\\\ 6 & 7 & -3 \\\\ 9 & 12 & -7\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n \n\nIf $D=LU$ is the LU decomposition of the matrix $D$ given above, what is the value of ${l}_{21}\\cdot {u}_{22}?$" :question/worked-solution "Let's apply our standard LU factorization algorithm.\n\nWe reduce the matrix $D$ to row echelon form to obtain the matrix $U,$ as usual. However, instead of writing zeros below the main diagonal, we will instead write down the entries of the matrix $L.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & -4 & 4 \\\\ 6 & 7 & -3 \\\\ 9 & 12 & -7\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & -4 & 4 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 5 \\\\ 9 & 12 & -7\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & -4 & 4 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 5 \\\\ -3 & 0 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\nL=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,U=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & -4 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nFinally, since ${l}_{21}=-2$ and ${u}_{22}=-1,$ we get\n\n$$\n{l}_{21}\\cdot {u}_{22}=(-2)\\cdot (-1)=2.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186411902 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119798 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d216cc0e-58a7-5fab-b5fe-60c7656338cc" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Missing Numbers in the Matrix L of an LU Factorization"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "356112b3-af6d-54d6-ab1f-e2dfccf01495" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411878} {:answer/id #uuid "369402a8-b0ec-5b9f-8768-00441214f23a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411879} {:answer/id #uuid "c1b1d085-a7b1-5e88-b3c0-1e9f61d1ce85" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411888} {:answer/id #uuid "c3b2d7a3-ff5f-5959-ad6f-ad71afdde67b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411889} {:answer/id #uuid "fab822a6-dc94-51a0-a04d-c63e1b31e7cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411895}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fab822a6-dc94-51a0-a04d-c63e1b31e7cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411895} :answer-field/id #uuid "07cd249d-c567-51b0-aec1-9ef9737fb65f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411896}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7fabcc7a-c8df-55fd-9125-ba1a0668699c" :question/math-academy-id "q-32802" :question/problem "$$\n{{\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 6 & 9 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 5 & 2\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{A}={{\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ \\boxed{} & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{L}\\cdot {{\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{U}\n$$\n\nConsider the LU factorization of the matrix $A$ above. What is the value of the entry ${l}_{21}$ in the matrix $L?$" :question/worked-solution "We want to make $0$ at the position ${a}_{21}$ using Gaussian elimination. To do this, we take the $2$nd row of $A,$ and we add the $1$st row of $A$ multiplied by $-3:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 6 & 9 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 5 & 2\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 5 \\\\ 4 & 5 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe entry ${l}_{21}$ of the matrix $L$ is the factor next to ${R}_{1},$ taken with the opposite sign:\n\n$$\n{l}_{21}=-(-3)=3.\n$$"}]}
